ClawWork — SuperClaw's model-relay coding harness
=================================================

This directory is a HARD FORK of the Pi coding agent
(https://github.com/earendil-works/pi), taken at tag v0.79.10.

Upstream is MIT-licensed; see LICENSE (Copyright (c) 2025 Mario Zechner).
That license and copyright are retained in full and continue to apply to
the code derived from Pi.

As of this vendoring, ClawWork is maintained INSIDE SuperClaw — it is no
longer a tracking fork of an external repository:

  - the upstream git history has been dropped (this is a v0.79.10 snapshot,
    not a branch that rebases onto Pi);
  - SuperClaw owns and evolves it from here (no automatic upstream pulls);
  - the bundled harness is gitignored at build time (node_modules/, dist/)
    and produced by `scripts/build-clawwork.sh`.

SuperClaw additions layered on top of the v0.79.10 snapshot:

  - config-only rebrand in packages/coding-agent/package.json
    (name "@superclaw/clawwork", bin "clawwork", piConfig dir ".clawwork");
  - extensions/superclaw-governance.ts — the policy-snapshot governance
    extension the SuperClaw backend loads via `-e` (fail-closed posture
    enforcement: denylist > allowlist > pay/scan hard gates > read-only mode);
  - spikes/ — merge/contract gates run before changes land.

SuperClaw's own code (the Python kernel, backends, surfaces) is licensed
separately under the SuperClaw repository's terms.
